er"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","abstract":[{"text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"is_arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds). A "},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"code":"predecessors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is "},{"code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Arborescence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set of vertices of any size, the empty set included (Berge, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hypergraphs"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 1989). Not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no shared parent with one: a hyperedge is not an edge. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" module’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidenceGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a hypergraph as its bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"typ